      "judge": [
        {
          "check": "root-cause",
          "criterion": "root-cause@1",
          "input": "[BUG]\nAsking for next week's events makes event.list end with an error and a problem opens. The cause is that RANGE_RULES has no next_week entry, so rangeBounds reads undefined.offset and throws a TypeError. Asking for this week or all events still works.\nfiles: src/events.ts\n\n[TICKET_GOALS]\n1. Fix TypeError in rangeBounds (src/events.ts:40): RANGE_RULES lacks \"next_week\" (offset 1), though EventRange and the UI allow it, so event.list with range \"next_week\" crashes. Add the rule, and make unknown/invalid range values be rejected with an AppApiRejection (invalid_input) plus reportProblem(\"invalid_range\", ...) instead of throwing a TypeError. Add a test for next_week.\n\n[EVIDENCE_FILES]\nsrc/events.ts",
          "verdict": "root_cause",
          "quote": "RANGE_RULES lacks \"next_week\" (offset 1)",
          "quote_found": true,
          "judge": "judge@1",
